# BioBand Core Rules

## Stack
- Expo SDK 57 (React Native 0.86, React 19.2), development builds via EAS —
  not Expo Go: `react-native-audio-api` is a native module Expo Go cannot load
- Read the versioned docs at https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/ before
  touching an Expo API (see AGENTS.md)
- TypeScript strict mode
- React Navigation (bottom tabs → native stacks)
- i18next for all UI strings (en, tr, de — keep the three locale files in step)
- Dark theme via `src/theme/colors.ts`

## Development Workflow
- `npm run check` (typecheck, lint, Jest) must pass before a commit
- Prefer a pure, unit-tested function over logic buried in a hook
- Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before changing `src/audio/` or `src/instruments/`

## Code Style
- Functional components only
- No hardcoded UI strings — use `useTranslation()` and the locale JSON files
- Reuse existing components and theme tokens
- Comments explain *why*, in English

## File Organization
```
src/
  audio/        # Shared AudioContext, scheduler, offline render, encoding
  instruments/  # Engines, samples and song charts per instrument
  hooks/        # Screen-facing hooks over engines and storage
  components/   # Shared UI, grouped by instrument
  screens/      # Screen components
  navigation/   # Navigators
  storage/      # AsyncStorage + expo-file-system persistence
  supabase/     # Optional cloud sync
  i18n/         # Translations
  theme/        # Colors
  types/        # TypeScript types
```
